hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1670","Narrated Abu Umamah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is nothing more beloved to Allah than two drops and two traces: A teardrop shed out of fear of Allah"""""
"1671","Narrated Al-Bara' bin 'Azib: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Bring me a shoulder blade or tablet.\"" Then he wrote: Not equal are those of believers who sit. 'Amr bin Umm Maktum who was behind him said: \""Is there an exemption for me?\"" So the following was revealed: Except those who are disabled. There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas"""""
"1672","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: A man came to Prophet (ﷺ) seeking permission to go for Jihad. So he said: 'Do you have parents (living)? ' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then it is for them that you should perform Jihad.'\ [Abu 'Eisa said:] There is something on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. (One of the narrators) Abul-Abbas is the blind (Al-A'ma) poet (Ash-Sha'ir)"""""
"1673","Narrated Al-Hajjaj bin Muhammad: That Ibn Juraij commented on Allah's saying: Obey Allah and obey the Messenger"
"1674","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If the people knew what I know about being alone"""""
"1675","Narrated to us Ziyad ibn Ayyub — narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun — informed us al-Walid ibn Jamil — from al-Qasim Abu 'Abd al-Rahman — from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n> *\The best of charities is the shade of a tent [sheltering] in the Cause of Allah"""","""" a servant granted [for service] in the Cause of Allah"""","""" or a noble stallion [loaned for use] in the Cause of Allah.\""""""""*\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhī) said: *\""""""""This is a ḥasan"""","""" ṣaḥīḥ"""","""" gharīb hadith"""","""" and it is more authentic in my estimation than the hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ.\""""""""*\n\nTransliteration of the chain (isnād):\n*Ziyādu bnu Ayyūba — Yazīdu bnu Hārūn — al-Walīdu bnu Jamīl — al-Qāsimi Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Abū Umāmah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu)*\n\nNote: The term \""""""""ṭarūqat faḥl\"""""""" (طَرُوقَةُ فَحْلٍ) refers to a noble male camel or stallion held in reserve for breeding or riding"""","""" loaned or dedicated in the Cause of Allah — a means of ongoing benefit (ṣadaqah jāriyah). The word *ṭarūqah* denotes a female camel impregnated by a noble stallion"""","""" and by extension the term here signifies a prized"""","""" serviceable animal contributed for the sake of Allah"""","""" subḥānahu wa taʿālā."""""""""""
"1676","Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \War is deceit.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""""
"1677","Narrated Abu Ishaq: \I was next to Zaid bin Arqam when he was asked: 'How many battles did the Prophet (ﷺ) fight ?' He said: 'Nineteen.' So I said: 'How many battles did you take part in with him ?' he said: 'Seventeen.' I said: 'Which of them was the first?' He said: 'Dhat Al-Ushaira' or Al-'Usaira'. '\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""""
"1678","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) positioned us during the night at Badr.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There is something on this topic from Abu Ayyub. This Hadith is Gharib"""""
"1679","Narrated Ibn Abi Awfa: \I heard him saying\"" - meaning the Prophet (ﷺ) - \""while supplicating against the Ahzab: 'O Allah"""""
"1680","Narrated by Abū ʿAmmār al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth, who narrated from al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from Yazīd ibn Abī Maryam, who said: ʿAbāyah ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ met me while I was walking to the Friday prayer and said, \Rejoice"","" for these steps of yours are in the path of Allāh.\"" He added"","" \""I heard Abū ʿAbs say that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whosever two feet become dusty in the path of Allāh"","" they shall be forbidden to the Fire.'\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan gharīb ṣaḥīḥ hadīth. Abū ʿAbs' name is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jabr. In this chapter"","" there are narrations from Abū Bakr and another Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAbū ʿĪsā further stated: Yazīd ibn Abī Maryam is a Syrian man from whom al-Walīd ibn Muslim"","" Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah"","" and others from the people of Shām narrated. Burayd ibn Abī Maryam is from Kūfah; his father was a Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" and his name is Mālik ibn Rabīʿah. Burayd ibn Abī Maryam heard from Anas ibn Mālik"","" and from him narrated Abū Isḥāq al-Hamdānī"","" ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib"","" Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq"","" and Shuʿbah."""""
"1681","Narrated Yunus bin 'Ubaid: the freed salve of Muhammad bin Al-Qasim said: \Muhammad bin Al-Qasim sent me to Al-Bara' bin 'Azib to ask him about the flag of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'It was a black square of Namirah.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""""
"1682","Narrated Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufrah: From one who heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: ""If you suffer a surprise attack from the enemy then say: 'Ha Min, they will not be victorious.'"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There is something on this topic from Salamah bin Al-Akwa'. This is how some of them reported it from Abu Ishaq, the same as the narration of Ath-Thawri. And it has been reported from him, from Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufrah from the Prophet (ﷺ) in Mursal form"
"1683","Narrated Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufrah: From one who heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: \If you suffer a surprise attack from the enemy then say: 'Ha Min"""""
"1684","Narrated 'Uthman bin Sa'd: That Ibn Sirin said: \I made my sword like the sword of Samurah bin Jundab. Samurah claimed that he made his sword like the sword of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""""
"1685","Narrated Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : \During the year of the conquest"""""
"1686","Narrated Anas bin Malik: \The Prophet (ﷺ) rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. He said: 'There is nothing to be frightened of"""""
"1687","Narrated Anas bin Malik: \There was a cause of fright in Al-Madinah. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) borrowed a horse of ours called Mandub. He said: 'I have not seen anything to be frightened of"""""
"1688","Narrated Anas: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was the nicest person among the people"""""
"1689","Narrated Abu Ishaq: From Al-Bara' bin 'Azib who said: \A man said to us: 'Did you flee from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) O Abu 'Umarah ?'\"" He said: \""No"""""
"1690","Narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Indeed"","" the spirits of the martyrs are in green birds that feed upon the fruits of Paradise or the trees of Paradise.\""\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."""""
"1691","It was narrated from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\The first three to enter Paradise were presented to me: a martyr"","" a chaste person who guards his chastity"","" and a servant who worshipped Allah excellently and was sincere to his masters.\""\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: \""This is a hasan hadith.\"""""""
"1692","Narrated Anas: \The hand-guard on the sword of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was made from silver.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. This is how it has been reported from Hamam from Qatadah from Anas. While some of them reported it from Qatadah"""""
"1693","Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Luḥayʿah narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Dīnār, from Abū Yazīd al-Khawlānī, that he heard Ḍaʿālah ibn ʿUbayd say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say:\n\n\The martyrs are four:\n\nFirst: A man of sound faith who met the enemy and was truthful before Allah until he was killed. He is the one toward whom the people shall raise their eyes on the Day of Resurrection in such a manner.\"""""""" And the Prophet"""","""" peace and blessings upon him"""","""" raised his head until his cap (qalansuwah) fell off. ʿUmar said: \""""""""I do not know whether he meant the cap of ʿUmar or the cap of the Prophet"""","""" peace and blessings upon him.\""""""""\n\nSecond: A man of sound faith who met the enemy"""","""" and it was as though his skin had been struck by the thorns of a talḥ tree out of cowardice. Then a stray arrow came and killed him. He shall be in the second rank.\n\nThird: A man of faith who mixed righteous deeds with sinful ones. He met the enemy and was truthful before Allah until he was killed. He shall be in the third rank.\n\nFourth: A man of faith who was excessive against himself (i.e."""","""" committed sins). He met the enemy and was truthful before Allah until he was killed. He shall be in the fourth rank.\""""""""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""""""""This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith. We do not know it except from the narration of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Dīnār.\""""""""\n\nHe said: \""""""""I heard Muḥammad (i.e."""","""" al-Bukhārī) say: 'Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated this hadith from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Dīnār"""","""" and he said it was from the shaykhs of Khawlān"""","""" and he did not mention in it the narration from Abū Yazīd.' And ʿAṭāʾ ibn Dīnār was considered reliable (laysa bihi baʾs).\""""""""\n\n*Peace and blessings be upon the Messenger of Allah"""","""" his family"""","""" and his Companions.*"""""""""""
"1694","Narrated Anas bin Malik: The Prophet (ﷺ) entered (Makkah) during they year of the Conquest"
"1695","Narrated 'Urwah Al-Bariqi: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Goodness will remain in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Judgement: (They bring about) Rewards and spoils of war.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Umar"""""
"1696","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blessing of the horse is in its redness.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib"""""
"1697","Narrated Abu Qatadah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The best horse is the black one with a spot on the face"""""
"1698","Another chain with similar meaning. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib Sahih"
"1699","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) disliked Shikal in horses. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Shu'bah reported similarly from 'Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khath'ami"
"1700","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arranged for the Mudammar among horses to race from Al-Hafiya' to Thaniyyah Al-Wada'"""""
"1701","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \No stake is acceptable except in archery"""""
"1702","Narrated Abu Ad-Darda': That he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: ""Seek your weak for me. For indeed you sustenance and aid is only by your weak."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1703","Narrated Abu Ad-Darda': That he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: \Seek your weak for me. For indeed you sustenance and aid is only by your weak.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""""
"1704","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The angels do no accompany a group among whom there is a dog or a bell.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Umar"""""
"1705","Qutaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n*\No one is wounded in the cause of Allah — and Allah knows best who is truly wounded in His cause — except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the colour of blood and the fragrance of musk.\""""""""*\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: *\""""""""This is a hasan sahith (good and authentic) Hadith"""","""" and it has been narrated through multiple chains from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""""""""*\n\n- """""""""""
"1706","Narrated Umm Al-Husain Al-Ahmasiyyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivering Khutbah during the farewell Hajj"
"1707","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Hearing and obeying is required from every Muslim man - in what he like and what he dislikes - as long as he is not ordered with disobedience. If he is ordered with disobedience"""""
"1708","Narrated Abu Yahya:From Mujahid from Ibn 'Abbas who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited instigating fights between beasts"""""
"1709","Narrated Jabir: \The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited branding on the face and striking (it).\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""""
"1710","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\There is no one among the people of Paradise who would be pleased to return to the world except the martyr"","" for he would love to return to the world"","" saying"","" 'So that I may be killed ten times in the cause of Allah"",""' due to what he sees of the honor that Allah has bestowed upon him.\""\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a sahih (authentic) hadith."""""
"1711","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah, from Anas"
"1712","Narrated Abu 'Ubaidah: That 'Abdullah said: \On the Day of Badr when the captives were gathered"""""
"1713","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \The idolaters wanted to purchase the body of a man who was from the idolaters. But the Prophet (ﷺ) refused to trade with them [for him].\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib"""""
"1714","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Messenger of Allah sent us on a military expedition"""""
"1715","Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):\n\nHe said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Whoever meets Allah without any trace of jihad"""","""" he shall meet Allah with a deficiency (thalmah) upon him.\""""""""\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a *gharib* (uncommon/singular) hadith in the narration of al-Walid ibn Muslim from Isma'il ibn Rafi'. And Isma'il ibn Rafi' was considered weak (*du'afā'*) by some of the scholars of hadith.\n\nHe (Abu 'Isa) further said: \""""""""I heard Muhammad (i.e."""","""" Imam al-Bukhari) saying: He is a trustworthy narrator (*thiqah*)"""","""" whose hadith is of a sound standard (*muqārib al-ḥadīth*).\""""""""\n\nThis hadith has also been reported through other chains of narration from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAs for the hadith of Salman (may Allah be pleased with him)"""","""" its chain of narration is not connected (*muttaṣil*)"""","""" for Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir never met Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nThis same meaning has also been reported through the chain of Ayyub ibn Musa → Makḥul → Sharāḥbil ibn al-Simṭ → Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) → the Prophet (ﷺ)"""","""" in a similar narration.\n\n*Note: This hadith is recorded by al-Tirmidhi in his Sunan and is classified as* gharib *due to the weakness of Isma'il ibn Rafi' in the chain"""","""" though alternative chains corroborate its meaning.*"""""""""""
"1716","Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived from Tabuk"""""
"1717","Muhammad ibn Bashshar, Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi, and others narrated to us, saying: Safwan ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The martyr feels nothing from the touch of death except as one of you feels from the sting of a flea.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih gharib hadith."""""
"1718","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Jamil al-Filastini informed us, from al-Qasim Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \There is nothing more beloved to Allah than two drops and two traces: a drop of tear shed in fear of Allah"","" and a drop of blood shed in the cause of Allah. As for the two traces"","" one is a trace left in the cause of Allah"","" and the other is a trace left in the performance of one of the obligatory duties of Allah.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan gharib hadith."""""
"1719","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Messenger of Allah sent us on a military expedition"""""
